      "id": "claim_2ee16d6ae0b24f8cb2ce6876e260452a",
      "statement": "State appetite rules can impose earlier or stricter risk controls without enlarging delegated authority: Texas requires a roof inspection at or above 15 years and does not permit binding at or above 25 years, while the Matrix separately requires referral at or above 25 years and line authority remains capped at $800,000.",
